From 1554dd7fc11004c377cee3b21614db8c3dd50f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:35:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07186/11362] [outer-loop] CORRIGENDUM: SGE smoke-test level
 tracking was reporting an unenforced floor, not real progress
 (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-5)

Found while checking whether cd82's reflection advice actually
changed subsequent proposals (operator: "do that"). Direct inspection
of action_log in every artifact scripts/outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py
has ever produced -- 7 real-GPU runs from the original 2026-07-10
g50t run through this session's 3-game REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-4 re-test --
shows level_before/level_after = 0 on EVERY logged action, in EVERY
run, on all 3 games. The real environment level never left 0, not
once.

Root cause: run_game() initialized max_level = prior_levels (an
informational label from ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml describing what
OTHER solve methods, GameAdapters and banked trajectories, have
reached for that game) and folded real observations into that SAME
variable via max(max_level, after_level). This harness has never
seeded the env at prior_levels -- no GameAdapter, no trajectory
replay, just a bare env.reset(). Since prior_levels was always >= the
real level ever observed, max_level_reached silently reported the
assumed starting point forever, independent of what the run actually
did. Every prior write-up (chat summaries, ops/known-issues.md task 6
entries) reported this artifact as if it were a measurement.

Fixed: run_game() now tracks real_initial_level/real_max_level_observed
honestly from the observed trajectory, independent of prior_levels/
target_level (now documented as informational-only via a
methodology_note field). leveled_up is computed strictly from the
real trajectory. Every existing artifact (9 files, including both
5699-3/5699-4 baseline snapshots) was retroactively patched with the
corrected fields + a corrigendum note, preserving the original
(misleading) fields unmodified alongside the correction. Result:
real_initial_level=0, real_max_level_observed=0, leveled_up=false for
all 7 runs -- a starker, more honest null than what was reported
("0/3 escaped level 0 at all," not "0/3 escaped their assumed L1/L2
starting point").

Does NOT invalidate the REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3/5699-4 mechanism findings
(nudge firing, parse-rate improvements, cd82's strategy-text language
genuinely shifting toward the advised action type after each
reflection) -- those are facts about router internals verified
directly from diagnostics_log, independent of this level-tracking bug.

4 new tests (fake env/policy, no GPU) verifying the counting logic
directly, including the exact bug scenario (real level never
advances despite a much higher prior_levels label). Spec:
REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-5 with its own scenario + spec-declaration test.

